      "anchor": "q_t(x,t) + A q_x(x,t) = 0; q : R × R → R^m; A is a constant m × m real matrix",
      "observation": "The referenced linear problem is a homogeneous, first-order, constant-coefficient system in one space variable x and time t, with an m-component real-valued unknown."
    },
    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 23; printed page 1; paragraph following equation (1.1)",
      "anchor": "subscripts are used to denote partial derivatives with respect to t and x",
      "observation": "The symbols q_t and q_x denote temporal and spatial partial derivatives."
    },
    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 25; printed page 3; opening discussion of hyperbolicity",
