          "The assertion identifies a PDE as a conservation law with a specified flux; it does not assert existence, uniqueness, initial data, or boundary data (printed pages 3–4, selected sentence and equations (1.1), (1.8)).",
          "The specified flux is exactly linear, f(v) = Av, without an added constant or explicit dependence on x or t (printed page 4, opening sentence)."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "undebatable_constraints": [
    "Preserve the m-component real system and constant m × m real matrix from equation (1.1); the source is not restricted to m = 1 (printed page 1, equation (1.1) and following paragraphs).",
    "Preserve the stated flux f(v) = Av and the spatial derivative of its composition with q (printed page 3, equation (1.8); printed page 4, opening sentence).",
    "Preserve the homogeneous equation with zero right-hand side and the time-plus-space derivative structure (printed page 1, equation (1.1); printed page 3, equation (1.8)).",
    "Do not present discontinuous-field or integral-form equivalence without additional interpretation: the source separately qualifies passage from integral to differential form by smoothness (printed page 4, Sections 1.1.1–1.1.2)."
